{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791416022,"nonce":"7wuoBz4GEeIZFM2d9gL6bIKvU9U=","title":"Unarchived by default everywhere a program runs: include_archive is the opt-in","message":"Every jq program runs over every issue, the archived included, and only the default program filters them out. So a custom query on the command line, in a flow or in a view sees the archived unless its author remembers the select, and a store that has consolidated duplicates holds an archived copy of every one of them: such a query sees double. Decided: the input a program runs over is the unarchived issues, and `--include-archive` / `include_archive=False` puts the archived back, on the list, the log, every view kind that takes a query and the Starlark mirrors of each. Design document first: doc/design/include-archive.md.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["cli","tui","core"],"priority":"high","status":"to-do","type":"story"}}]}